From 643ea3309d2df951dabba32bdd26384223d9eacf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Super Z <dev@local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:44:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add --io-cache ram: process-wide raw-GGUF tensor cache for
 slow storage

On Colab/Drive/HDD the streaming passes re-read the packed expert tensors
from disk on every pass (pool collection, refit, artifact write). Now the
raw packed tensors are copied to RAM on first touch (lazily, tensor by
tensor, ~= packed file size) and served from a process-wide cache afterwards.

- hf_gguf_to_hf.py: GgufHfSource(cache_ram=...), shared _RAW_CACHE, stats
- hf_stream.py: BlockStreamRunner(io_cache=...), block-load time accounting,
  io-cache summary in close()
- hf_pipeline.py: --io-cache {disk,ram}, wired into both runners + profile
- hf_field_transform.py: write_field_artifact(io_cache=...)
- test_io_cache.py / test_io_cache_stream.py: bit-exactness + cache-hit tests
- README.md: Speed knobs section + Colab note

Verified on mini-OLMoE GGUF: logits bit-identical disk vs ram, second
instance fully served from RAM.
